{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>This is the statute.</b> This passage too was spoken in the wilderness of Sinai, when HaShem commanded and they sent [them] out of the camp, and at Passover there were those impure through corpse contact. And this passage was juxtaposed because it pertains to the priest." "<b>A red cow, whole.</b> That it not be small. The Gaon [Saadia] said that the waters of lustration are like honey: they harm one of red bile and benefit one of moist [bile]. And there is no need."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:18:21.648838174Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}